# Git hooks are executed by bash, which treats a CR as part of the command and
# dies with "$'\r': command not found" followed by a syntax error. This repo has
# core.autocrlf=true, so without this rule the checked-out hook is CRLF and the
# pre-commit proof-number gate cannot run AT ALL -- it fails before it reaches
# its first check, which reads like a passing commit rather than a skipped gate.
#
# Found 2026-07-30: tests/test_check_proof_numbers.py's two end-to-end hook tests
# were failing for this reason while the checker itself was fine.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
